# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sanity settings — where each value goes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1) The public website (this folder) has NO build step, so it can't read a
#    .env file. Its values go directly in js/config.js:
#
#      SANITY_PROJECT_ID: "your-project-id"   (from sanity.io/manage)
#      SANITY_DATASET:    "production"
#      SITE_URL:          "https://www.your-domain.com"   (optional; used for
#                          canonical/share links. No slash at the end.)
#      CMS_STUDIO_URL:    "https://your-studio.sanity.studio"  (after deploying
#                          the Studio; powers the footer "Owner login" link)
#
#    The project id and dataset are public, not passwords.
#
# 2) The Sanity Studio (studio/ folder) reads studio/.env — copy
#    studio/.env.example to studio/.env and fill in:
#
#      SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
#      SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=production
#
#    These must match js/config.js.
#
# NEVER put a Sanity API token (read or write) in js/, in any HTML file, or in
# this file. The website only reads published posts from Sanity's public CDN
# and needs no token. The dataset must be "Public" in sanity.io/manage.
#
# Also allow the website's address under sanity.io/manage > API > CORS origins
# (e.g. https://www.your-domain.com and http://localhost:8000 for testing).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
